WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.770
In 1875, John Henry Newman
wrote about a toast.

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.400
He would drink to the Pope, if you please.

3
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:11.380
But to conscience first,
and to the Pope afterwards.

4
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:15.680
But consciences differ, across
cultures and across eras.

5
00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.720
So if your conscience tells
you to do something wrong,

6
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.710
should you still follow it?

7
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.220
In this mission, you'll
climb Thomas Aquinas' ladder:

8
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:28.290
three steps from reason to
a judgement about one act.

9
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.870
Then you'll set his
account beside other views,

10
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:36.130
religious and non-religious, from
Butler and Newman to Freud and Fromm.

11
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.740
Your mission: find out whether a conscience
that might be mistaken should still

12
00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:41.560
be followed.
